      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-31_WidnesExaminer_art0049" n="art0049">
        <head>WHICH COMPRISE</head>
        <p>WHICH COMPRISE</p>
        <p>THE Earlestown and Newton Examiner, and Ashton Golborne, and Haydock Reporter, published Friday elternoon. The district is in the heart of the Lancashire coal field.</p>
        <p>THE St. HelenB Examtner and Preseot Weekly News, published Friday afternoon. The district ccmprises the Centre of the Glass, Chemical, and Watch Trades of the Kin Ma, &amp;C.</p>
        <p>THE Runcorn Examiner, published Friday after- noon. lt is the only Weekly Paper in the district. and Offers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers.</p>
        <p>THE Widnes Examiner, published Friday after- noon. Widnes contains the largest number of Chemical Workpof any town in the kingdom, and is rapidly becoming iti important centre of industry. Auction. Education, Wanted, To be Let, On Sale, Legal Public Meeting, Sermon, Lecture, Bazaar, and other Public notices, Advertisements (exceptParliamentary)are inserted in %lithe above papers at one charge.</p>
        <p>Each of the above papers consists of 8 pages. 58 long an Wide columns,each column admitting more matter than th Columns of any otherlocal paper—a fact deserving the eke n tion of both advertisers and subscribers. Each Exammer in ddition. to giving the local intelligence of the district. in Which it circulates, contains the general news of the week.</p>
        <p>Price of each Paper—ONE PENNY. Advertisers have thus the opportunity of WIDE PUBLICITY AT A CHEAP RATE.</p>
        <p>Advertisements received at any of the District Offices or may be sent to the Chief Office, Warringt2n. Stamps received for amounts under ss.</p>
