      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-31_WidnesExaminer_art0088" n="art0088">
        <head>PADGATE.</head>
        <p>PADGATE.</p>
        <p>LECTURE —An interegting lecture on home mission work was delivered on 'Yednesday evening in the church schoolroom. by the F. IT. Powell, organizing secre- tary of the Additional Curate Society. There was a good attendance and the lecture which was illustrated with the aid of the hydro-oxygen lantern was well appreciated by those present. A vote of thanks to the Rev. F. B. Powell concluded the meeting. CHOIR SERMONS.—The annual sermons in connection with the church choir were preached in Christ Church, Podgate, on Sunday. The service was conducted,morh" ing and evening, by the Rev. J. J. Longhorn. vies!. The anthem which was effectively rendered by the ohm!, in•the morning, was "Clap your hand.% 0 ye peoto. and in the evening "Give glory unto the Lord." Nei; tories were taken at the close of each service en behalf oi the choir funds.</p>
